<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 4.1 PCT IN JULY - C.BANK.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 4.1 PCT IN JULY - C.BANK.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 6.18 billion zlotys, or 4.1 percent, in July to 157.47 billion after a 2.0 percent rise in June, preliminary central bank figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Broad money grew 16.0 percent in the January-July period.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		  JULY	JUNE	  JULY '96</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	   4.1	2.0		 2.3</p>
<p> Money in bln			 157.47   151.28(151.16)  119.58</p>
<p> Foreign currency (in bln PLN)   28.18    26.43 (26.39)   21.97</p>
<p> National currency		  129.28   124.85(124.77)   97.62</p>
<p> Cash in circulation		 27.83    26.84	     22.49</p>
<p> Lending to non-financial sector 96.59    94.27 (94.31)   65.16</p>
<p>NOTE - revised figures in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
